{"name":"Chocolate Oatmeal","hex":"#b5a39c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"chocolate","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A food made from ground roasted cocoa beans.","A drink made by dissolving this food in boiling milk or water."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of or containing chocolate.","Having a dark reddish-brown colour/color."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chocolate"},{"term":"oatmeal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Meal made from rolled or round oats.","A breakfast cereal made from rolled oats, cooked in milk or water."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a light greyish brown colour, like that of oatmeal."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oatmeal"}],"entries":[{"title":"Chocolate","blocks":[{"text":"Chocolate is a food made from roasted and ground cocoa beans. It can be a liquid, solid, or paste. It is eaten on its own and used to flavor other foods."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Three_Bars_%281%29.jpg/330px-Three_Bars_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chocolate"},{"title":"Oatmeal","blocks":[{"text":"Oatmeal is a preparation of oats that have been dehusked, steamed, and flattened, or a coarse flour of hulled oat grains (groats) that have either been milled (ground), rolled, or steel-cut. Ground oats are also called white oats. Steel-cut oats are known as coarse oatmeal, Irish oatmeal, or pinhead oats. Rolled oats were traditionally thick old-fashioned oats, but they can be made thinner or smaller and may be categorized as quick oatmeal or instant oatmeal depending on the cooking time required, which is determined by the size of the oats and the amount of precooking."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Oatmeal.jpg/330px-Oatmeal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","